  "individualFlowReview": {
    "ca8d4075-1f15-40f9-9432-667e0a033660": "Re-reviewed for b425 receipt adoption: the authority module changes only the exact approved receipt SHA literal. The verifier still reads bounded ordinary files through canonical-parent and symlink/link-count checks, then compares opened file metadata before and after reading. The new receipt digest does not supply a pathname and cannot relax these checks.",
    "9886fba1-1186-4e41-b1fa-6a6877440237": "Re-reviewed both changed contexts individually: src/db.ts changes only an error annotation from any to unknown plus an erased structural assertion before the existing optional code read; emitted path handling is unchanged. The maintenance test consolidates named and default imports of the same node:fs/promises module without changing values. The child receives a fixed forwarder.db filename within the parent test-created private temporary directory as a separate process argument; no remote request chooses this fixture path.",
    "f2f8ea59-c823-49ff-8d81-50ae176c845a": "Re-reviewed line 45 PRAGMA index_xinfo: the interpolated index name comes from index_list of fixed fixture tables in the freshly created local test database. Database context changed only an erased catch error annotation/assertion; it adds no SQL interpolation or external input. The existing locally generated index-name provenance and SQL bytes are unchanged.",
    "db0f006d-1b47-43d9-8b35-86ae5ee08f58": "Re-reviewed line 51 PRAGMA foreign_key_list: names come from sqlite_master in the same private test-created schema, with JSON.stringify retained at the existing boundary. No request-supplied database or identifier enters this fixture. The db.ts change is an erased error type annotation/assertion unrelated to schema names or SQL execution; the original finding remains scoped to this controlled test flow.",
    "4494650c-4f77-4efc-9956-2a491467ddaf": "Re-reviewed command execution against the adopted authority digest: only the approved receipt SHA literal changed. The operator-selected Python executable remains absolute, canonical and an ordinary file; spawnSync still uses separate fixed -I/-B/-c bridge arguments, shell:false, timeout and bounded output. Receipt content cannot become a shell command or create its own approval entry. No command boundary changed.",
    "7039073d-34a6-4901-9897-4c0a40ca7b0a": "Re-reviewed the line 85 file flow: canonical parent, ordinary file, no symlink, nlink=1, bounded size, read-only/no-follow open and pre/post-read identity checks remain unchanged. The authority change only replaces the independently approved exact digest in the same read-only mapping/profile key. It cannot select a new path or bypass file checks."
  },
